# MDCN Communication Hierarchy & Account Map

This document outlines the hierarchical communication structures, message visibility rules, and the active SoftHat accounts (IDs and Keys) available for the Military Distributed Communication Network (MDCN).

## 1. Network Architecture & Communication Flow

The MDCN utilizes a 3-layer architecture governed by Solidity smart contracts.

```mermaid
graph TD
    %% Strategic Layer
    subgraph Strategic Layer [Strategic Command - Tier 1]
        A[Army Command]
        N[Navy Command]
        AF[Air Force Command]
    end

    %% Operational Layer
    subgraph Operational Layer [Operational Command - Tier 2]
        OA[Army Ops]
        ON[Navy Ops]
        OAF[Air Force Ops]
    end

    %% Tactical Layer
    subgraph Tactical Layer [Tactical Units - Tier 3]
        TA1[Army Field Unit 1]
        TA2[Army Field Unit 2]
        TN[Navy Field Unit]
        TAF[Air Force Field Unit]
    end

    %% Communication Flows (Top-Down Commands)
    %% Army
    A -->|Commands| OA
    A -->|Commands| TA1
    A -->|Commands| TA2
    OA -->|Commands| TA1
    OA -->|Commands| TA2
    
    %% Navy
    N -->|Commands| ON
    N -->|Commands| TN
    ON -->|Commands| TN
    
    %% Air Force
    AF -->|Commands| OAF
    AF -->|Commands| TAF
    OAF -->|Commands| TAF
    
    %% Field Data & Maintenance (Bottom-Up Reporting)
    TA1 -.->|Field Data| OA
    TA1 -.->|Field Data| A
    TN -.->|Field Data| ON
    TN -.->|Field Data| N
    TAF -.->|Field Data| OAF
    TAF -.->|Field Data| AF
    
    %% Intelligence Sync (Lateral & Vertical)
    A <==>|Intelligence| OA
    OA <==>|Intelligence| TA1
    N <==>|Intelligence| ON
    ON <==>|Intelligence| TN
    AF <==>|Intelligence| OAF
    OAF <==>|Intelligence| TAF
    
    classDef strategic fill:#bbdefb,stroke:#1565C0,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef operational fill:#c8e6c9,stroke:#2E7D32,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef tactical fill:#ffcdd2,stroke:#B71C1C,stroke-width:2px;
```

### 1.1 Who Can Send to Whom?
- **Commands ([MDCNCommand.sol](file:///a:/MDCN-Military-Distributed-Communication-Network/Contracts/MDCNCommand.sol)):** Top-down only. 
  - Strategic (Layer 1) can send to Operational (Layer 2) and Tactical (Layer 3).
  - Operational (Layer 2) can send to Tactical (Layer 3).
  - Tactical (Layer 3) **cannot** send commands.
- **Field Data & Maintenance ([MDCNTactical.sol](file:///a:/MDCN-Military-Distributed-Communication-Network/Contracts/MDCNTactical.sol)):** Bottom-up reporting.
  - Tactical (Layer 3) logs field events and maintenance statuses to Operational or Strategic recipients.
- **Intelligence ([MDCNCoordination.sol](file:///a:/MDCN-Military-Distributed-Communication-Network/Contracts/MDCNCoordination.sol)):** Lateral and Vertical.
  - Any node can sync intelligence with any other node across the network (e.g., Tactical to Strategic, Strategic to Strategic, Army to Navy).

### 1.2 Who Can View Which Messages?
- **Recipients:** A node can only view messages where they are the explicit `recipient` address or if the message was broadcasted to their [RecipientGroup](file:///a:/MDCN-Military-Distributed-Communication-Network/src/components/CommandSection.js#30-36) and [Branch](file:///a:/MDCN-Military-Distributed-Communication-Network/src/components/CommandSection.js#29-30).
- **Sender:** A node can always view the history of messages they have dispatched.
- **Immutability:** Once a message is sent and stored on the blockchain, it is immutable. Acknowledging a message triggers a secondary blockchain transaction that marks the initial message as `Acknowledged` (`🔒 Immutable`).

---

